<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#hellanodikai">Glossary</a> · Term · office</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hellanodikai</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hellanodikai, 'judges of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a>', were the officials who organised and judged the ancient Olympic Games. Chosen from the citizens of Elis, they supervised the athletes' training, enforced the rules, fined offenders and awarded the olive wreaths. Their number changed over time, settling at ten from the 4th century BCE, and they wore purple robes.</p></div>
